# settlement-api: the Spec Gate and the Merge Gate. Branch
# protection on main enables "Require review from Code
# Owners", so a pull request merges only with an approval
# from the owner of every path it touches. GitHub reads this
# file from the base branch. The last matching pattern takes
# precedence, so the catch-all comes first.

# Merge Gate: every change, REVIEW.md included.
*                    @acme/settlement-change-owners

# Intent: the durable spec and its executable contracts.
/specs/              @acme/settlement-change-owners
/tests/contracts/    @acme/settlement-change-owners

# Guardrails, the jobs that judge a change, the build
# targets those jobs run, and ownership itself.
/.claude/            @acme/factory-platform
/.github/            @acme/factory-platform
/.gitlab-ci.yml      @acme/factory-platform
/Makefile            @acme/factory-platform
/.github/CODEOWNERS  @acme/settlement-change-owners

# Workbench. The constitution belongs to the Change
# Owners; rules and skills to the domain team; hooks,
# settings, and agents stay with the platform team above.
/CLAUDE.md           @acme/settlement-change-owners
/.claude/rules/      @acme/settlement-engineers
/.claude/skills/     @acme/settlement-engineers
